<title>INDIA: Indian metals markets closed for holiday.</title>
<headline>Indian metals markets closed for holiday.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indian metals' markets were closed on Thursday for a local Hindu festival, dealers said.</p>
<p>On Wednesday, ready copper was steady at 11,800 rupees per quintal and nickel at 38,600 rupees. On Tuesday, copper fell by 50 rupees and nickel by 200 rupees.</p>
<p>A dealer said that reports of improving world markets also curbed the fall. &quot;Market may rise on fresh demand,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>The markets reopen on Friday.</p>
<p>-- Bombay Commodities +91-22-265 9000</p>
</text>
